 // The parallel-move primitive. FPRs hold doubles (8 bytes, ABI-SPEC 7.7);
-// a "32-bit float" stack slot is written as the full double, as on ARM64.
+// a "32-bit float" stack slot is written and read as the full double
+// (stfd/lfd), so every FPU value in a Dart stack slot is in double format
+// (ConstantInstr::EmitMoveToLocation follows the same rule). Native (C ABI)
+// single-format slots are written only by the EmitNativeMove* hooks.
 // There are no quad slots (no SIMD). Clobbers R0 (Load/Store), FpuTMP for
 // double stack-to-stack, and the allocator's temporary for word
